# CI/CD Rollout Ownership — Fix in PM, Not in the Repo

SSOT: `codex/05-infrastructure/cicd-setup.md`. Full flow: `codex/08-workflows/ci-cd-flow.md`

## The Core Rule

Before changing ANY CI workflow or quality gate file in a service repo, ask:
**"Does this fix belong in PM and propagate to all 65 repos?"**

If yes, make the change in PM. If you fix it in just one repo, the other 64 stay broken
and the fix will be overwritten the next time a rollout runs.

## What Is Owned in PM (Never Edit Per-Repo)

| Per-repo file | Real owner in PM | Propagation |
| ------------- | ---------------- | ----------- |
| `.github/workflows/quality-gates.yml` | `.github/workflows/python-quality-gates.yml` or `ui-quality-gates.yml` (reusable workflow) | `rollout-quality-gates-ci-workflows.py --workflow-call` |
| `scripts/quality-gates.sh` (logic) | `scripts/quality-gates-base/base-service.sh` or `base-library.sh` or `base-ui.sh` | Instant — sourced live at runtime |
| `.prettierignore` (shared rules) | `scripts/quality-gates-base/.prettierignore-base` | Instant — inherited via base script |
| CI env vars (CLOUD_MOCK_MODE, CLOUD_PROVIDER, GCP_PROJECT_ID) | `python-quality-gates.yml` job-level env | Rollout |
| `cloudbuild.yaml` | `configs/cloudbuild-*-template.yaml` | `rollout-cloudbuild.py` |
| `buildspec.aws.yaml` | `configs/buildspec-*-template.yaml` | `rollout-buildspec.py` |

## What IS Per-Repo (Edit in the Repo)

- `scripts/quality-gates.sh` **config** (SERVICE_NAME, SOURCE_DIR, MIN_COVERAGE, LOCAL_DEPS) — stub only
- `.github/workflows/quality-gates.yml` `on:` branch filters — repo-specific
- `.github/workflows/quality-gates.yml` `dep_repos:` input — derives from manifest `dependencies[]`
- Repo-specific prettier ignores beyond the shared base

## Rollout Script Reference

```
# Patch CI workflow env vars / flags across all repos:
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-ci-workflows.py

# Regenerate thin workflow_call callers from manifest (after reusable workflow changes):
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-ci-workflows.py --workflow-call

# Single repo:
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-ci-workflows.py --repo <name>

# Dry run first:
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-quality-gates-ci-workflows.py --dry-run

# Cloud Build (services, APIs, UIs):
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-cloudbuild.py [--dry-run] [--repo <name>]

# Cloud Build + wheel-only libraries:
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-cloudbuild.py --include-library [--dry-run]

# CodeBuild (AWS):
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/propagation/rollout-buildspec.py [--dry-run] [--repo <name>]

# Pre-build auth validation (run before builds to fail fast on missing credentials):
python3 unified-trading-pm/scripts/validation/validate-build-auth.py [--gcp-only] [--aws-only] [--check-secrets]
```

## Anti-Patterns — NEVER Do These

NEVER: Edit a per-repo `quality-gates.yml` to add/fix an env var → fix `python-quality-gates.yml`
NEVER: Add a gate check to a per-repo `quality-gates.sh` → add to `base-service.sh`
NEVER: Make a per-repo workaround so one repo's QG passes → fix the root cause in the base
NEVER: Add `pip install ruff` or any tool install to a per-repo CI step → fix in `python-quality-gates.yml` or `setup-python-tools/action.yml`
NEVER: Edit `.prettierignore` in one repo for a shared pattern → add to `.prettierignore-base`
